        "label": "What excites you about this opportunity?",
        "type": "textarea",
        "canonical_field": "essay:generated:question_4468289007",
        "action": "fill",
        "value": "The part I would want to work on is data infrastructure that has real consequences for real users. At Summer Atlantic Capital I built major parts of the ML and data core of an anomaly-detection system: the repository and CI scaffold, the event-ingestion pipeline, a versioned FastAPI microservice, and the public detection API, plus temporal sequence modeling over event streams and a learning-to-rank layer for prioritizing alerts. What I learned there is that model performance is only half the problem. An anomaly system that fires too often just creates a second problem, so prioritization, explanation, and failure modes matter as much as accuracy. That maps closely to consumer finance, where decisions about credit affect people who have the least room to absorb a bad call. Perpay serving 500,000+ customers with subprime credit means the pipelines are load-bearing, not decorative. I also like that Perpay is profitable and a B Corp, because it suggests the incentives behind the data work are aimed at customer outcomes rather than volume. I want to own a substantial piece of a system, not isolated tickets.",
